# ── HTML documents: always revalidate ────────────────────────────────────────
# This has to exist for the immutable rules below to be safe. index.html is what
# names the ?v= of every script and stylesheet, so a stale copy of it keeps
# pointing at the PREVIOUS asset URLs — and those are now pinned for a year.
# Cache the HTML and the page freezes completely: new deploy, old markup, old
# assets, no expiry that will ever release it.
#
# no-cache does not mean "do not store". It means "store it, but revalidate
# before serving". The round trip is a 304 with no body when nothing changed,
# which is cheap, and correctness here is worth more than one conditional GET.
#
# Every SPA route is listed because the Worker answers each of them with
# index.html, and a _headers rule matches on the REQUEST path, not on the file
# that ends up being served. Keep this list in step with SPA_ROUTES in
# worker/index.js.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
